{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Organic run evidence (2026-08-15): Gerrit Verified run 31892203411 for change 1809 PS3 passed in 31m59s with 2-4s job queues. macOS was the completion critical path: job 30m18s; default 1545.29s (25m45s), integration 155.01s (2m35s). No individual test exceeded 30s; the slowest macOS node was test_hook_falls_back_to_git_when_env_unset at 26.11s, followed by the locked N=3000 import benchmark at 23.06s. Ubuntu default/integration were py3.11 419.68/76.22s, py3.12 468.30/86.96s, py3.13 637.29/83.10s. Successful-job occupancy was 4,368s (72m48s). Operations over 30s were the four default phases, four integration phases, optional-extras isolation 95s, and tickets-history mount 45s.\\n\\nAncestry caveat: the exact tested ref was refs/changes/09/1809/3 = 250c623334, whose sole parent is 588d7df0bd. git merge-base --is-ancestor rejects both 8f9e40efcc and 0f34e8dc3b as ancestors. Therefore this run does not contain the landed build-provenance fixture optimization and cannot be counted as a current-code steady-state sample. It nevertheless strengthens the empirical long-tail finding: queueing was negligible and the 25m45s macOS default phase had no single >=30s test, so this slow run is distributed host/suite throughput variation rather than an individual-test long pole."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786808991488490001,"uuid":"66d88b27-4923-4d1f-b9f9-fe23f64a8a3d"}